      "type": "open_ended",
      "question": "How has the role of the Business Identification Number (BIN) evolved from its initial implementation in 2017 to its current status within the Authorized Economic Operator (AEO) framework?",
      "answer": "Initially, as seen in the 2017-06-01 factory inspection standards, the BIN served primarily as a static identifier for VAT compliance and facility verification. By 2024, under the AEO Rules 2024, its role expanded into a dynamic requirement for the AEO lifecycle, including application, tier-upgrading, and renewal, ultimately becoming a tool for intelligence reporting and registry management by 2025.",
